# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# merged_works_labeled.db is a ~20 GB SQLite corpus and is deposited on
# Zenodo rather than carried in git. Ignore the directory contents but keep
# its README (which documents the schema and how to obtain the file) and the
# two small stage-05 outputs that stage 06 and the Supplementary Information
# read. `data/*` rather than `data/` so git still descends into the directory
# and can see the negations below.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/interim/
data/interim/*
!data/interim/citshare_h3x4entities.csv
!data/interim/fractional_citations_by_country_h3.csv
# The slim published corpus lives on Zenodo (10.5281/zenodo.22791584), not in
# git: at 1.2 GB the compressed file is well over GitHub's 100 MB limit. Keep
# only its README and the checksums that let a downloader verify the deposit.
!data/published_dataset/
data/published_dataset/*
!data/published_dataset/README.md
!data/published_dataset/SHA256SUMS.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Databases
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit a database by accident, wherever it sits in the tree. Nothing is
# exempt: the published corpus is distributed through Zenodo, not GitHub.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

